[statement]
Over an installed set, apk's ranking of candidates is not an order: the
installed `a` (no version, `k:10`) outranks `cc` (a version), `cc`
outranks `bb` (no version, `k:20`), and `bb` outranks `a`. apk takes the
candidates in turn, the installed one first, then the repository's in the
order listed, keeping the better of each pair: `a` gives way to `bb`, and
`bb` to `cc`. Contrast `-cc-bb`.

[repository]
P:bb
V:1
p:v
k:20

P:cc
V:1
p:v=1

P:b
V:1

[installed]
P:a
V:1
p:v
k:10

[world]
v

[request]
b

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove a 1
install b 1
install cc 1
